{
  "case_id": "2008-08-310",
  "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: It's not often that we have disagreements as to the basic facts. The red brief says that the tax in question constitutes 11 percent of the tax base, and you talk about that in the reply brief. Can you spend just a little bit of time at the outset telling us your views of this tax? And although it's the Respondent's statement and not yours, do you think 11 percent of the tax base means 11 percent of"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Polar Tankers, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Valdez vessel tax violates the Constitution's Tonnage Clause because it operates as a charge on a privilege of trading in the port of Valdez, and that tax is apportioned in a way that is guaranteed to tax extraterritorial values and values that do not have a connection to the city. That violates the Due Process and Commerce Clauses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Polar Tankers, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is a tax that is directed exclusively at vessels and not on all vessels. It's -- by exempting small boats and all boats that are engaged in commercial fishing and all boats that dock exclusively at city-owned harbors. This is a tax, a property -- it's calls a property tax, but it's a tax that falls only on vessels and is directed at those vessels, that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Well, do you -- do you take the position -- let's say that if the State of Alaska taxed all the other property you had mentioned except for the tankers and the city taxed the tankers, that that would by definition be discriminatory tax and/or on some other basis violate the Tonnage Clause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: How many days."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: But you don't think a daily -- a daily charge on vessels for remaining in port violates the Tonnage Clause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "The Court has so held on several occasions that a flat fee violates the Tonnage Clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: What State is being discriminated against in the scenario we have before us today?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ultimately, it's not going to be the oil companies that pay this tax; it's going to be purchasers of oil."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: I thought you said earlier or implied earlier that we couldn't draw a distinction, really, between capacity and value because tonnage in the 18th century was simply a proxy for the -- for the value of the ship?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the Wheeling case, this Court said it is too well settled to question the taxes upon vessels based upon their value as property do not violate the Tonnage Clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Alaska",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0001-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State of Alaska imposes an oil and gas tax on property used in the oil and gas extraction, transportation, et cetera, business, but it also authorizes a city under Section 43.56 and 29.45 -- the City of Valdez may impose that tax as well."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Wait a minute, owed to the State for what? What would be owed to the state? It's still a State tax and they are the collection agent, and it's a -- a credit against what they owe for their collections, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Alaska",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. OLSON: The taxpayer, once he pays $10 to the city under this tax, doesn't have to pay $10 to the State under this tax because he gets a credit for --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Well, that's exactly the question I wanted to ask you. Supposing the city did not impose any taxes on anybody except the people who pay this tax, and that's all. Would it -- would it be constitutional or unconstitutional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But is it -- do you -- do you contest the point that was made in the reply brief that back at the end of the 18th century, tonnage was considered a proxy for value, that it was the customary mode of measuring the value of a ship?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Is a porthole tax in your view okay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Rothfeld",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROTHFELD: But it -- it is imposed by the State. The State decides decide what subject it has. It identifies the property that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Rothfeld",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "To -- to address Justice Ginsburg's question as to whether there were other taxes like this, we have not found any other tax anywhere that has been imposed singling out vessels as -- for -- for property taxation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: What about the -- the broader tax situation at the -- at the -- in -- in 1789? Did -- did ports have sources of -- or exercise the authority at that time to tax property generally, e.g., real estate in the city to support the activities of the ports, or were they dependent solely upon things like import-export taxes, et cetera?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: So -- so that the argument they are taxing other things, therefore it's okay to tax this, would have been an argument just as potent in the 18th century or impotent, as the case may be, as it is now?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: How -- under your view, how is a city supposed to impose a property tax on a vessel?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Rothfeld",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROTHFELD: My -- my understanding is that real estate certainly was subject to tax and that ports would have the authority to tax other types of property. Vessels were set aside as a particular item by the Tonnage Clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: So -- so you think we should resolve the tax by seeing how generally applicable property taxes are in Valdez?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-310",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "879a9c1be495b32d614baf533f515db0b3ef65380fe046fe75391acbc6c5ed7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-879a9c1be495-0003-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:20 a.m., the case in the above-entitled case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
